{
  "id": "R013Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "MRI scan",
  "description": "An MRI (magnetic resonance imaging) scan creates detailed internal images of your body using magnetic fields and radio waves, no radiation exposure. This outpatient procedure excels at imaging soft tissues, organs, and the brain. You lie still in the MRI scanner for 20-60 minutes while hearing loud knocking sounds. Depending on your doctor's questions, contrast dye may be injected through an IV to highlight certain structures. The procedure is painless. Results accurately diagnose tumors, infections, injuries, or neurological conditions. You go home immediately with no side effects. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on the imaging protocol used. Options include without contrast and with contrast.",
